-- src:252 | khoẻ hoặc thần kinh, theo thời gian, tuổi tác.
DECLARE `A kind of accident` IS ONE OF
    `an accident at work`
    `an accident in daily life`
    `a traffic accident`

DECLARE `The accident` HAS
    `the date`                                                       IS A DATE
    `where it happened`                                              IS A `A country group`
    `sudden`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by an external and visible force on the body`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `outside the insured person's will and control`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the direct cause of the death or the injury`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury was the first consequence of the accident`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury was an accumulation of accidents or injuries`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury was caused, directly or indirectly, by the aggravation of a weakness, defect, degeneration or illness that existed before cover began` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury was caused solely by the accident, not by illness, declining health or nerves, time or age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the kind`                                                       IS A `A kind of accident`
    `serious`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a third party was involved`                                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- Definition 20: the five marks of a chronic illness.
-- src:100 | 20. Bệnh mãn tính (Bệnh mạn tính)
-- src:101 | Là bệnh tật có một trong các đặc tính sau đây:
-- src:102 | Diễn biến từ từ và điều trị không thể khỏi dứt điểm
-- src:103 | Bản chất là sẽ tái đi tái lại
-- src:104 | Hiện chưa có một phương pháp điều trị nào thích hợp
-- src:105 | Có thể dẫn đến thương tật/tàn tật vĩnh viễn
-- src:106 | Cần khám, xét nghiệm, điều trị hoặc theo dõi dài hạn
DECLARE `A mark of a chronic illness` IS ONE OF
    `it develops gradually and treatment cannot cure it completely`
    `by its nature it recurs`
    `there is at present no suitable treatment for it`
    `it may lead to permanent injury or disability`
    `it needs long-term examination, tests, treatment or monitoring`

