    `an invoice gives only a combined total`            IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The claim`

-- One claim: the person, the policy, the event, the items, the filing, other insurance,
-- and what has already been counted against each limit earlier in the period.
DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    `the insured person`                         IS A `The insured person`
    `the policy`                                 IS A `The policy`
    `the event`                                  IS A `The event`
    `the items`                                  IS A LIST OF `A claim item`
    `the filing`                                 IS A `The filing of the claim`
    `other insurance`                            IS A MAYBE `Other insurance`
    `already counted earlier in the period`      IS A LIST OF `An amount counted against a limit`

-- One item read in the light of its claim. The rules of Parts 2-4 take this.
DECLARE `An item of a claim` HAS
    `the claim`   IS A `The claim`
    `the item`    IS A `A claim item`

