§§ `Parties and acts, for the duties of Parts 4 and 5`

DECLARE `A party` IS ONE OF
    `the insured person or the heir`
    `PTI, the insurer`
    `the hospital`

DECLARE `An act` IS ONE OF
    `notify PTI of the claim`
    `submit the claim file`
    `submit the further documents`
    `gather the further medical information at own cost`
    `return the certificate and the insurance card`
    `present the insurance card and an identity card or passport`
    `sign the treatment documents`
    `pay the costs beyond the cover before leaving the hospital`
    `confirm the guarantee of payment`
    `pay the hospital directly`
    `have the insured person examined by an independent medical establishment`
    `require an autopsy`
    `appoint an independent claims adjuster`

§§ `Outcomes`

-- Why an item is not within the cover, before any exclusion is asked about.
DECLARE `A reason an item is not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the insured person is not a person PTI insures`
    `the benefit was not bought`
    `the event is outside the period of insurance`
    `the event or the treatment is outside the geographical scope`
    `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
    `the head of cost is not one the benefit pays`

-- What Parts 2-4 make of one item.
DECLARE `The outcome for an item` IS ONE OF
    `not covered`         HAS `the reason`       IS A `A reason an item is not covered`
    `excluded`            HAS `the exclusions`   IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `in a waiting period` HAS `the last day`     IS A DATE
    `payable`             HAS `the amount`       IS A NUMBER

-- What the Rules make of a whole claim.
DECLARE `The outcome for a claim` IS ONE OF
    `refused in full, the claim being filed late`
    `assessed`  HAS `the outcomes for the items` IS A LIST OF `The outcome for an item`
                    `the total payable`          IS A NUMBER

-- An input the Rules make impossible: rejected, not answered.
DECLARE `A problem with the schedule` IS ONE OF
    `an optional benefit was bought without Programme II`
    `the sub-limits of Programme II add up to more than its main limit`
    `the sub-limits of Programme I add up to more than its main limit`
